{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbCb877uEHDkL3opL9Tg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: APPROVE\n\nNo P1 or P2 findings. Every acceptance criterion is met: the script covers all three backends with resume, the fixtures cover answer, tool calls, resume and error for each backend, and the probe answers are on #4 with the Claude read-only fallback decision. I also grepped the committed fixtures at HEAD for the home-directory name and found no leak.\n\n- P3 #4 probe comment — it still says `PR: #PRNUM` — edit it to `#18`.\n- P3 scripts/record.sh:51 — `sed \"s/$USER/user/g\"` treats `$USER` as a regex. An empty or short `$USER` mangles every fixture — use `sed \"s|$HOME|/Users/user|g\"` or guard against an empty value.\n- P3 scripts/record.sh:46 — `sleep \"$CANCEL_AFTER\"` runs the full duration even if the CLI exits early, and `kill` then errors on the dead pid. Harmless, but add `|| true` or check the pid with `kill -0`.\n- P3 scripts/record.sh:41 — the argv file leaves out the prompt, and the cursor prompt is appended only after the file is written. Fixtures can't be reproduced from their argv — save the prompt as `NAME.prompt`.\n- P3 scripts/record.sh:53 — a cursor session id is never printed, so resuming cursor needs a hand-dug id from the result line — print it, or note it in the header.\n\nSTATUS: DONE"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":365,"cache_read_input_tokens":44611,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":365},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dfd18ba-a3ed-4a44-bd90-c4ca03e8efdd","uuid":"3b3b94c4-0e68-4d6f-9e7d-7898a29ee037","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:27:44.054Z","request_id":"req_011C